{"metadata":{"description":"Safety-gated SSH development plugin for DeepSeek Harness and MCP, built for GPU and offline laboratory servers.","id":"gh:1339210349","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"deepseek-harness-ssh","slug":"gdgfd22/deepseek-harness-ssh","topics":["deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh-plugin","gpu","mcp","offline-server","ssh","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Safety-gated SSH development plugin for DeepSeek Harness and MCP, built for GPU and offline laborato"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"d SSH development plugin for DeepSeek Harness and MCP, built for GPU and offline laboratory servers."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-lab-ssh"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Safety-gated SSH development tools for DeepSeek Harness and standard MCP clients."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"The plugin lets an agent running on a connected workstation use a laboratory server's GPU, runtime, "},{"id":"p5s2","text":"and explicitly configured source workspace while the server remains isolated from the public interne"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"d explicitly configured source workspace while the server remains isolated from the public internet."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Version `0.3.0` is an experimental preview. Pin a tested DeepSeek Harness version before laboratory "},{"id":"p6s2","text":"3.0` is an experimental preview. Pin a tested DeepSeek Harness version before laboratory deployment."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"This is an independent community plugin and is not an official DeepSeek AI package."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Why it exists"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Giving an agent a normal SSH terminal exposes arbitrary destinations, commands, and filesystem paths"},{"id":"p9s2","text":". This project inserts a deny-by-default policy layer:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- fixed model-visible host aliases;
- pinned OpenSSH SHA256 host-key fingerprints;
- environment, lo"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"cal-key-file, or SSH Agent credential references;
- per-host command allowlists, auto-approval rules"},{"id":"p10s3","text":", and deny rules;
- bounded command output and timeouts;
- alias-based remote directory roots with c"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"anonical containment checks;
- bounded UTF-8 reads and atomic, hash-protected writes;
- optional ali"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"as-based command working directories;
- a disabled-by-default HTTPS artifact bridge for offline serv"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"ers;
- one JSON policy shared by DeepSeek Harness and Codex MCP."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The plugin does not expose arbitrary hosts, interactive shells, inline secrets, unrestricted file tr"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ansfer, delete/move/chmod operations, background commands, port forwarding, reverse tunnels, or agen"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"e/move/chmod operations, background commands, port forwarding, reverse tunnels, or agent forwarding."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Status"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The DeepSeek Harness plugin, stdio MCP server, command policy, restricted SFTP access, working-direc"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"tory aliases, and first artifact-bridge layer are implemented. The test suite contains 25 tests acro"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"ss 9 files and never contacts real laboratory infrastructure or the public internet."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Visual short-lived credential sessions, persistent audit, role-based policy, directory sync, depende"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"ncy closure, caching, and resumable transfer remain future work."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Requirements:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- Node.js `^22.19` or `>=24`;
- DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.7` or a compatible `0.1.x` preview;
- pnp"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"m on `PATH` for `dsh plugin`."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Build and install:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Copy the example configuration outside the repository, replace every placeholder, and point the DSH "},{"id":"p20s2","text":"configuration outside the repository, replace every placeholder, and point the DSH user patch at it:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Set credential environment variables in the same process that starts DSH:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"See the Chinese operator guide and Chinese quick start for configuration, approval policy, offline a"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"rtifact staging, and troubleshooting."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- `ssh_list_hosts`: list redacted configured host aliases.
- `ssh_list_file_roots`: list directory a"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"liases and access policy.
- `ssh_list_directory`: list bounded entries under an authorized root.
- `"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"ssh_read_file`: read bounded UTF-8 text and return its SHA256.
- `ssh_write_file`: create or atomica"},{"id":"p26s4","text":"lly replace bounded UTF-8 text.
- `ssh_exec`: run an allowlisted command on a fixed host and optiona"},{"id":"p26s5","text":"l directory alias.
- `ssh_stage_artifact`: approval-gated download, verification, and atomic upload "},{"id":"p26s6","text":"s.
- `ssh_stage_artifact`: approval-gated download, verification, and atomic upload of one artifact."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Offline servers"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The artifact bridge is not a transparent proxy. The workstation accepts an HTTPS URL without credent"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ials or query tokens, validates every redirect against an administrator domain allowlist, enforces a"},{"id":"p28s3","text":" size limit and mandatory trusted SHA256, then atomically creates the file inside an explicitly arti"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"fact-enabled remote root. Existing files are not replaced."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Generic SOCKS/HTTP proxying, SSH forwarding, and reverse tunnels remain out of scope so server netwo"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"rk isolation is preserved."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Codex MCP"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The repository contains the safe empty `config/lab-ssh.empty.json` and project-level `.codex/config."},{"id":"p31s2","text":"toml`. Build the package and reload Codex in a trusted project to discover the MCP server. For real "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"deployment, point a private Codex configuration at a JSON file outside the repository."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The server can also be started directly:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## Develop and verify"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"On Windows, run a clean-room acceptance test that reclones the public repository into the system tem"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"porary directory and reuses neither the current dependencies, build output, DSH profile, nor private"},{"id":"p36s3","text":"d reuses neither the current dependencies, build output, DSH profile, nor private SSH configuration:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"It runs `npm ci`, type checking, tests, build, package inspection, isolated-profile plugin installat"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"ion, and a DSH Web HTTP smoke test with `hosts: []`. Port `3180` is used by default, and the tempora"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"ry environment is removed afterward."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Review SECURITY.md before publishing. Real SSH configuration, credentials, logs, local profiles, bui"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"ld output, and archives must not be committed or included in a release."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}
